<!-- Status-bar small icon: TigerDuck paw-in-disc, from
     tigerduck-simple-android.svg (Illustrator export).

     Android keeps ONLY the alpha channel here and re-tints the result, so the
     paw cannot be painted white on top of the disc: white and black are
     equally opaque, and the icon would flatten to a solid circle. The paw is
     therefore knocked out of the disc, as one compound path with an evenOdd
     fill whose detail subpaths punch transparent holes. Do not split this
     into separate path elements and do not change fillType.

     The group scales the source disc (19.08 of a 26.16 viewport, i.e. 17.5dp)
     up to Material's 20dp circular keyline so it matches sibling status-bar
     icons. Drop the group to get the artwork at its exported size.

     fillColor is duck yellow to match the brand, but it is PREVIEW ONLY:
     it changes how this file looks in Android Studio and nowhere else. On
     device the RGB is thrown away with the rest of the colour information,
     and the status bar always draws the icon in its own foreground colour.
     The lever that actually tints anything is setColor() on the builder.

     The full-colour logo is set via setLargeIcon and appears in the
     notification body. -->
